## Residual risk (accepted)

Under **`drop`**, live Timescale may lag until `sync_timedb` catches up from disk; silent live gaps are expected when queues are full. Under **`pause`**, long DB stalls grow RabbitMQ ready-queue depth (and broker memory/disk). Unexpected race drops of sample *k* can still leave carry reflecting *k−1* while *k+1* is written with a skewed delta (first-writer-wins); sync_timedb repairs missing *seconds* from disk but cannot overwrite live-written keys.

